# Generated by tool/screenshots, which is tracked. The output is not, and that
# is deliberate rather than an oversight: fakes.dart derives its business dates
# from DateTime.now(), because the daily summary and reconciliation compute a
# business date the same way and read by exact path, so a hardcoded date would
# render those screens permanently empty. Re-running on a different day
# therefore moves about 39 of the 101 images with no code change behind any of
# them - measured on 2026-08-11 and recorded under "Standing traps" in PLAN.md.
# Tracking the output would put those 39 into every future diff. Regenerate with
# `flutter test --no-pub --concurrency=1 tool/screenshots`, and compare against a
# baseline generated the same day.
/screenshots/
screenshots.zip

# Scratch captures from an earlier session, kept locally rather than shared.
.codex-*.png

# Claude Code's permission rules. `.claude/settings.json` is tracked and shared -
# it is what stops every `flutter test` and `git diff` asking for approval. The
# `.local.json` beside it is per-machine, is written by the tool whenever an
# individual command is approved, and accumulates verbatim one-off entries that
# mean nothing on anyone else's machine.
/.claude/settings.local.json
